<title>USA: Kansas feedlot cattle market quiet, no sales - USDA.</title>
<headline>Kansas feedlot cattle market quiet, no sales - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DODGE CITY 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trade was quiet, with no sales slaughter steers or heifers confirmed, USDA said.</p>
<p>Inquiry and demand light. Sales confirmed for the week to date including late Friday and the weekend on 1,800 cattle. Bids and asking prices $66.00 and $69.00 per cwt, respectively.</p>
<p>Sales FOB feedlot net weights after 4 percent shrink.</p>
<p>Confirmed - none</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8720))</p>
